  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "The wreckage of a flying saucer or disc said to have crashed near Roswell, New Mexico, in 1947 is rumoured to have been taken to a lab at Wright-Patterson, an Air Force base in Ohio, and Michels notes that Neil McCasland, an Air Force general, later ran that very lab. Michels tells this himself across several episodes: once he adds Fort Worth as a stop on the route, once he calls the base, also home to Project Blue Book (the US Air Force's UFO study of the 1950s and 60s), the alleged home of the debris, and once he credits the musician Tom DeLonge and his book Secret Machines, saying the Air Force's work on studying captured foreign hardware ended up with the Roswell pieces, \"if you believe the lore.\" If true, it would put a crashed craft in the hands of one specific government lab."
}
